d expect to align their work and presentations in this class with a major project in their field. Students will give both individual and team talks.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Enrollment limited to: EN and BEE juniors and seniors or permission of instructor.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "two First-Year Writing Seminars and major affiliation.", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": ["Oral Communication/Presentations: Plan, devise, formulate, design, and report information via professional presentations for various technical and stakeholder needs.", "Written Communication: Identify, research, negotiate, and compose various texts to further a technical or engineering effort with consideration to context and audience; use writing and planning skills to support presentation work both for the talk itself and as archival legacy documentation.", "Visual and Multimodal Communication: Visualize, illustrate, and appropriately caption visuals; discriminate between methodologies for creating visuals other multimodal artifacts to support the technical endeavor; create visuals and multimodal artifacts that are accessible."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "EN", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2025FA, 2025SP, 2024FA, 2023FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2909, "crseId": 373380, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ENGRC", "catalogNbr": "3027", "titleShort": "Cross-cultural Comm & Ethics", "titleLong": "Cross-cultural Communications and Ethics in the Workplace", "crseAttrs": [], "c